 S~S  CHANGELOG metadata: "SimpleSal Time and Event Management" software.

=====================

    S~S NOTE: this release only: change in procedure for copying release notes to the change log.

------------------------------------------

    Lessons learned:  RELEASE/CHANGELOG edits.  Previously, editors copied the contents of release
    to the changelog AFTER the release file was edited; convention now is to copy the release note about
    the release (the previous release) to the changelog BEFORE editing the release file for this release.

    This results in the combined content of RELEASE (this) and CHANGELOG (past)
        telling the story completely without duplication.

    For this release only: in order to change the model,
        no edits to CHANGELOG occur in this release.

    Actually this process note will be added to CHANGELOG,
        but not as part of a release note.

------------------------------------------

    S~S NOTE: return now to normal programming, which is an accumulation of release notes over Time.
    At the time of the next release note being added, this process note need no longer be visible.
    The sequence of changes (process note exists and then does not) is visible in the repository App.

